Verdict: PASS. The diff does what #1036 asked (option (a), refuse), and running the real binary confirmed it. The verdict is written to session_plan/eval_task_1.md.

What I saw running the binary from a scratch directory:

• A config missing its closing quote (model = "claude-haiku-5-5): yoyo -p hi printed error: config file is malformed, named .yoyo.toml:1: unterminated quote, said how to fix it, and exited with code 2. Piped input did the same. Neither made an API call.
• Inspection still works: yoyo config get model on the same broken file printed the warning and exited 0. That's the intended split: you can still look at the file the error points to.
• A valid config isn't refused: with a clean .yoyo.toml, -p went straight to the usual "No API key found" (exit 1).

From reading the diff:

• Pure decision function: config_syntax_refusal decides; it returns nothing for a clean file, and its message is checked with exact full-string tests.
• Named exit code: the code is the constant CONFIG_SYNTAX_REFUSAL_EXIT = 2.
• Wiring: the check is wired into main.rs and into yoyo review, the only subcommand that calls a provider.
• Every new definition is used: each one added in the diff has a caller in the same diff.
• A real false positive was found and fixed: text inside a multi-line """/''' string was being checked as if it were config lines. The new test of valid TOML shapes, which also reads this repo's own .yoyo.toml, now covers that.
• Docs: common-issues.md describes the refusal, the exit code and how to fix it; ARCHITECTURE.md records the decision and the reason.

